            <ArticleTitle>Radiation Dosimetry of a Graphite Moderated Radium-Beryllium Source.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S110-S112</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Brookhaven National Laboratory Sigma Pile is a radium-beryllium neutron source imbedded in a cube of graphite blocks. The pile is approximately 2.13 m on four sides and is 3.07 m high. Thermoluminescent dosimeters were used to determine the neutron and gamma-ray dose rates in the pile. Gamma-ray dose rate measurements have also been made in the air outside of the pile, while the radium-beryllium neutron source was being withdrawn from the pile. The Monte Carlo code has been used to calculate the coupled neutron-photon transport. Measured dose rates at various locations agreed with the calculated values within 5% to 15%.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
